Subject: [PATCH] C13's follow-ups, patch 1 (cld-advisor, at main's word in
 M23, item 7): B1905'S SCRIPT WRITES ITS KEPT TABLE ONLY WHEN ASKED (--write);
 A RUN OF THE LOCK OR OF THE LEDGER'S GENERATOR WRITES NOTHING, AND TESTS HOLD
 BOTH

Main's M23, item 7: the script writes its kept table only when asked (--write); a run of the lock or of the ledger's
generator writes nothing, and a test holds that.

- sweep_tables.py (main's script): its one write, of sweep_tables.json, stands under `if "--write" in sys.argv[1:]`,
  with a dated comment; its docstring's line on what it writes says "with --write (2026-11-13)". Nothing else changes.
- B1905's lock: it compares main's script with main's copy in git's history, as C13's first patch made it; the
  comparison now takes this seat's two changes back first (`_as_main_gave_it`), so it still holds that the rest is
  main's, byte for byte, under a dated comment.
- Two tests. The script run as a program from a copy of its folder writes no table without --write and writes it with
  --write; the twin, main's script as handed over, writes it at every run. The lock's own reading of the script and the
  ledger's generator leave the kept table's time and bytes as they were.

BEFORE: on the script as it stood, the lock's new tests fail (the guard is not there); after, the arc's tests and the
ledger's: 18 passed.

0 of 19.
